{%- comment -%}
  Fixes the stray space before the comma preceding the year, e.g. "(non-archival) , 2025".

  In al_folio_core 1.0.15, `_layouts/bib.liquid` builds `entrytype` and appends
  `additional_info` through `markdownify`:

    {{ entry.additional_info | markdownify | remove: '<p>' | remove: '</p>' }}

  kramdown wraps the value as `<p>…</p>\n`, so stripping the tags leaves the trailing
  newline behind. A few lines later the layout joins on `", "`, producing "…\n, 2025",
  and HTML collapses that newline into a rendered space. The layout's closing
  `{{ periodical | strip }}` cannot help — the newline is interior to the string by then.

  This is the layout's own `_includes/hook/bib.liquid` extension point, which it renders
  after the `additional_info` capture and before the join. Liquid `include` shares the
  parent scope, so reassigning `entrytype` here takes effect in the layout. Entries with
  no `additional_info` never gain the newline, so this is a no-op for them.

  Fixing it here rather than by shadowing `_layouts/bib.liquid` is deliberate: `_layouts/`
  is on the style-contract stop list (`npm run lint:style-contract` fails if it exists),
  and this hook is a supported extension point rather than a copied file that must be
  re-synced on every gem bump. Remove this file if the gem starts stripping the value.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign entrytype = entrytype | strip -%}
